 "result": "Based on the subagent's report, these are the failures not attributed to the `partitioned` TypeError:\n\n1. **`tests/test_helpers.py::TestStreaming::test_async_view`**: `RuntimeError: Install Tessel with the 'async' extra in order to use async views` (raised at `src/tessel/app.py:1096`). The optional `asgiref` package isn't installed. This is a separate missing dependency.\n\n2. **`tests/test_request.py::test_limit_config`**: `assert None == 500000`. `request.max_form_memory_size` is `None`. The subagent suspects the installed Werkzeug lacks that feature (a 3.1+ addition), so it's likely the same version mismatch, but a different code path from `partitioned`. It wasn't confirmed directly.\n\n3. **`tests/test_helpers.py::test_open_resource_exceptions[a]`**: the subagent saw only truncated output (a `PytestUnraisable...` warning/error) and did not diagnose it, so its cause is unknown.\n\nThe count doesn't fully add up: the report lists about 20 `partitioned` failures plus these 3, against 24 failed and 1 error. Some of the 24 may not have been named individually, so I can't say for certain that no other non-`partitioned` failures exist. I can have the subagent re-check with `pytest -rf` and per-test tracebacks if you want an exact breakdown.",
